 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -11,16 +11,18 @@\n \n     Vectors need not be normalized (the evaluator normalizes them), but none may be\n     zero. The score is the minimum angle in degrees between any two points. This\n-    start draws uniformly random points with a fixed seed, so some pairs end up\n-    close together.\n+    implementation uses a Fibonacci lattice for a more uniform initial placement.\n     \"\"\"\n-    rng = random.Random(1)\n+    golden_ratio = 0.618033988749895\n+    golden_angle = math.pi * (3 - math.sqrt(5))\n     points = []\n-    for _ in range(n):\n-        z = rng.uniform(-1.0, 1.0)\n-        phi = rng.uniform(0.0, 2 * math.pi)\n-        s = math.sqrt(1.0 - z * z)\n-        points.append((s * math.cos(phi), s * math.sin(phi), z))\n+    for i in range(n):\n+        z = 1 - 2 * i / (n - 1) if n > 1 else 0.0\n+        r = math.sqrt(1 - z * z)\n+        phi = i * golden_angle\n+        x = r * math.cos(phi)\n+        y = r * math.sin(phi)\n+        points.append((x, y, z))\n     return points\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n \n",
